---
/**
 * Architecture of xauscalp. `compact` (home) shows three blocks; the full version (case study) adds the research chain.
 * Rendered as semantic HTML so it reflows on small screens and is readable by assistive tech.
 */
interface Props {
  compact?: boolean;
}
const { compact = false } = Astro.props;
---

<figure class:list={['flow', { compact }]}>
  <ol class="chain" aria-label="Architecture, left to right">
    {
      !compact && (
        <>
          <li class="node"><b>Data</b><span>Broker exports, coverage and quality checks</span></li>
          <li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
          <li class="node"><b>Features</b><span>Sessions, volatility regime</span></li>
          <li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</li>
        </>
      )
    }
    <li class="node"><b>Python research</b><span>Strategies propose; bid/ask backtest; walk-forward; reports</span></li>
    <li class="arrow" aria-hidden="true"><em>frozen rules</em>→</li>
    <li class="node ea"><b>MQL5 Expert Advisor</b><span>Read-only: signal → risk guard → decision log, inside MetaTrader 5</span></li>
  </ol>
  <div class="rail">
    <div class="parity"><b>Parity check</b><span>Same signals on the same data, session by session</span></div>
    <div class="veto"><b>Risk manager and hard limits</b><span>Fail-closed: any proposal it cannot verify is rejected, before any order</span></div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="sr-only">
    Python research produces frozen rules that run in a read-only MQL5 Expert Advisor, which writes a decision log. A parity check compares both. A fail-closed risk manager with hard limits sits between every proposal and any order.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .flow {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .chain {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: stretch;
  }
  .compact .chain {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
  .node {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    align-content: start;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: 16px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 4%, transparent);
  }
  .node.ea {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, transparent);
  }
  .node b,
  .parity b,
  .veto b {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .node span,
  .parity span,
  .veto span {
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .arrow {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    gap: 2px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 18px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .arrow em {
    font: 500 10px/1 var(--font-mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .rail {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .parity,
  .veto {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--line-strong);
  }
  .veto {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--signal) 60%, transparent);
  }
  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .chain,
    .compact .chain {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      grid-auto-flow: row;
    }
    .arrow {
      rotate: 90deg;
      padding: 2px 0;
    }
    .arrow em {
      rotate: -90deg;
    }
    .rail {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
